# No em dashes

Do **not** use em dashes (`—`, Unicode U+2014) anywhere in this project.

This applies to marketing copy, UI strings, docs, comments that mirror user-facing text, error messages, emails, and commit/PR descriptions.

## Use instead

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| `Less DMs—more sales` | `Less DMs. More sales.` or `Less DMs, more sales` |
| `One link—paid checkout` | `One link with paid checkout` or `One link. Paid checkout.` |
| `Whether you sell on WhatsApp—Instagram` | `Whether you sell on WhatsApp, Instagram` |
| `Plans from ₦3,000/month—no card needed` | `Plans from ₦3,000/month. No card needed.` |

## Allowed

- Hyphens in compound words: `shareable`, `first-time`, `link-in-bio`
- En dashes in numeric ranges only if required: `2024–2025` (prefer `2024 to 2025` in prose)
- Minus sign in code/math: `a - b`

## Before finishing copy edits

Search changed files for `—` and replace with a period, comma, colon, or rephrase.
